<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'">
<title>MSSQL {{if .Offline}}offline {{end}}schema {{if .History}}history{{else}}comparison{{end}} — {{if and .History .History.Baseline}}baseline captured{{else}}{{len .Differences}} difference(s){{end}}</title>
<style>
:root {
  color-scheme: light;
  --canvas: #eef1f4;
  --paper: #ffffff;
  --ink: #253344;
  --muted: #536170;
  --rule: #d4dbe3;
  --accent: #2a4d6d;
  --accent-wash: #eaf0f6;
  --removed: #8b2b36;
  --removed-wash: #fff1f2;
  --added: #245d3c;
  --added-wash: #edf6ef;
  --code: "Cascadia Code", "Consolas", "Liberation Mono", monospace;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { scroll-padding-top: 12px; }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--canvas); color: var(--ink); font: .875rem/1.5 "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif; }
main { width: calc(100% - 32px); max-width: 1440px; margin: 16px auto; padding: 24px 28px; background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
h1, h2, h3, p { margin: 0; }
h1 { font-size: 1.375rem; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 600; }
h2 { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.4; font-weight: 600; }
h3 { font-size: .8125rem; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 600; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
code, pre { font-family: var(--code); }
a { color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
a:hover { text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; }
.heading { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 16px; }
.subtitle { margin-top: 4px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .8125rem; }
nav { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: .8125rem; }
nav a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 32px; }
.status { margin-top: 12px; padding: 8px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--muted); font-size: .8125rem; }
.status strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
.status.equal strong { color: var(--added); }
.overview { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 24px; margin: 12px 0 20px; align-items: start; }
.inventory { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .8125rem; }
.inventory caption { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; padding-bottom: 4px; }
.inventory th, .inventory td { padding: 4px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.inventory th:first-child { padding-left: 0; text-align: left; }
.inventory th { font-weight: 600; }
.inventory tbody th { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; }
.mode { font-size: .8125rem; color: var(--muted); }
.mode p + p { margin-top: 4px; }
.mode strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
.mode code { color: var(--accent); }
.section-heading { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink); padding-bottom: 6px; }
.section-heading p { color: var(--muted); font-size: .75rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.change { padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); min-width: 0; }
.change-heading { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px 16px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.kind { color: var(--muted); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; overflow-wrap: anywhere; text-align: right; }
.metadata-change { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(200px, .85fr) minmax(0, 2fr); gap: 20px; align-items: start; padding: 10px 0; }
.metadata-change .change-heading { display: block; margin: 0; }
.metadata-change .kind { display: block; margin-top: 2px; text-align: left; }
.values { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; margin: 0; }
.values > div { min-width: 0; }
.values dt { font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 2px; color: var(--muted); }
.values dd { margin: 0; }
.values pre { margin: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; font-size: .8125rem; line-height: 1.5; }
.legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 16px; font-size: .75rem; margin: 0 0 4px; color: var(--muted); }
.legend .source { color: var(--removed); }
.legend .destination { color: var(--added); }
.sql-diff { margin: 0; padding: 6px 0; max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; background: var(--canvas); font-size: .8125rem; line-height: 1.45; tab-size: 4; }
.sql-diff code { display: block; min-width: max-content; }
.diff-line { display: block; padding: 0 8px; min-height: 1.45em; }
.diff-line.removed { color: var(--removed); background: var(--removed-wash); }
.diff-line.added { color: var(--added); background: var(--added-wash); }
.diff-line.hunk { color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-wash); }
.diff-line.file, .diff-line.note { color: var(--muted); }
.empty { padding: 16px 0; max-width: 70ch; color: var(--muted); }
.scope { margin-top: 24px; font-size: .75rem; color: var(--muted); max-width: 100ch; }
.scope h2 { color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px; }
.scope p + p { margin-top: 8px; }
.scope strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
.history { margin: 12px 0; font-size: .8125rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.history p + p { margin-top: 4px; }
.object-times { margin-top: 24px; }
.timestamps { table-layout: fixed; }
.timestamps th, .timestamps td { text-align: left; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.timestamps .kind { display: block; text-align: left; }
footer { margin-top: 20px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--muted); font-size: .75rem; }
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  main { padding: 20px; }
  .metadata-change { display: block; padding: 12px 0; }
  .metadata-change .change-heading { margin-bottom: 6px; }
}
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  main { width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 16px 12px; border: 0; }
  .heading { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 16px; }
  nav a { min-height: 44px; }
  .overview { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .change-heading { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 2px; }
  .kind { text-align: left; }
  .values { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 6px; }
}
@page { margin: 14mm; }
@media print {
  body { background: var(--paper); }
  main { width: 100%; margin: 0; max-width: none; padding: 0; border: 0; }
  nav { display: none; }
  .overview { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
  .metadata-change { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 2fr); gap: 16px; break-inside: avoid; }
  .metadata-change .change-heading { margin: 0; }
  .values { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 12px; }
  .sql-diff { overflow: visible; white-space: pre-wrap; }
  .sql-diff code { min-width: 0; }
  .diff-line { white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .change-heading, .legend { break-after: avoid; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main id="top">
<header>
  <div class="heading">
    <div>
      <h1>{{if .Offline}}Offline schema comparison{{else if .History}}Schema history{{else}}Schema comparison{{end}}</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Microsoft SQL Server · {{if .Offline}}Source / destination snapshot files{{else if .History}}Previous snapshot / current schema{{else}}Source / destination{{end}}</p>
    </div>
    <nav aria-label="Report sections"><a href="#differences">Differences</a>{{if .History}}<a href="#object-times">Object times</a>{{end}}<a href="#scope">Scope</a></nav>
  </div>
  {{if and .History .History.Baseline}}<p class="status"><strong>Baseline captured.</strong> No earlier snapshot exists; changes were not evaluated.</p>
  {{else if .Differences}}<p class="status"><strong>{{len .Differences}} difference(s) found.</strong> Review the source and destination values below.</p>
  {{else}}<p class="status equal"><strong>No differences found within the comparison scope.</strong></p>{{end}}
  {{with .Offline}}
  <div class="history">
    <p><strong>Source snapshot:</strong> <code>{{.Source.Database}}</code> on <code>{{.Source.Server}}</code></p>
    <p><strong>Source captured (UTC):</strong> {{.Source.CapturedAt}}</p>
    <p><strong>Destination snapshot:</strong> <code>{{.Destination.Database}}</code> on <code>{{.Destination.Server}}</code></p>
    <p><strong>Destination captured (UTC):</strong> {{.Destination.CapturedAt}}</p>
    <p>Compared local snapshot files only. No database connections; snapshot history is unchanged.</p>
    {{if .MigrationGenerated}}<p><strong>Migration SQL generated separately; not executed.</strong> Re-export/review destination drift before manual execution. Server/database guards do not detect schema drift.</p>
    {{else}}<p>Compare only: no migration SQL generated.</p>{{end}}
    <p>Results describe these two captures, not the current live databases. Capture times may differ; object timestamps are informational and are not compared.</p>
  </div>
  {{end}}
  {{with .History}}
  <div class="history">
    <p><strong>Database:</strong> <code>{{.Database}}</code> · <strong>Server:</strong> <code>{{.Server}}</code></p>
    {{if not .Baseline}}<p><strong>Previous snapshot (UTC):</strong> {{.PreviousAt}}</p>{{end}}
    <p><strong>Current snapshot (UTC):</strong> {{.CurrentAt}}</p>
    <p>Source = previous snapshot; destination = current schema. Added and removed objects are relative to the previous snapshot.</p>
    <p>Snapshots show net schema differences between captures, not a complete DDL audit or who made each change.</p>
    {{if .MigrationIncluded}}<p>Migration dependency/safety metadata included for offline generation. This capture does not generate or execute SQL.</p>{{end}}
  </div>
  {{end}}
  <div class="overview">
    <table class="inventory">
      <caption>Objects inspected</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Object group</th><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Destination</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Tables</th><td>{{.SourceTables}}</td><td>{{.DestinationTables}}</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Procedures, views, functions &amp; synonyms</th><td>{{.SourceObjects}}</td><td>{{.DestinationObjects}}</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <div class="mode">
      <p><strong>SQL comparison mode:</strong> <code>{{.Mode}}</code></p>
      {{if .Normalized}}<p>CREATE, ALTER and CREATE OR ALTER, including spacing before the module type, are normalized. Other text remains significant.</p>
      {{else}}<p>SQL definitions are compared as text. Formatting, comments and declaration differences remain significant.</p>{{end}}
      <p>Both modes normalize CRLF to LF. This report is read-only; no schema changes are applied.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
<section id="differences" aria-labelledby="differences-heading">
  <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="differences-heading">Differences</h2><p>{{len .Differences}} item(s)</p></div>
  {{range .Differences}}
  <section class="change {{if .SQL}}sql-change{{else}}metadata-change{{end}}" aria-labelledby="change-{{.Index}}">
    <div class="change-heading"><h3 id="change-{{.Index}}"><code>{{.Object}}</code></h3><span class="kind">{{.Kind}}</span></div>
    {{if .SQL}}
    <div class="legend"><span class="source">− Source lines</span><span class="destination">+ Destination lines</span><span>3 context lines · Original line numbers</span></div>
    <pre class="sql-diff" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="SQL diff for {{.Object}}"><code>{{range .Lines}}<span class="diff-line {{.Class}}">{{.Text}}</span>{{end}}</code></pre>
    {{else}}
    <dl class="values"><div><dt>Source</dt><dd><pre>{{.Source}}</pre></dd></div><div><dt>Destination</dt><dd><pre>{{.Destination}}</pre></dd></div></dl>
    {{end}}
  </section>
  {{else}}
  {{if and .History .History.Baseline}}<p class="empty">This capture is the starting point. Run snapshot mode again to compare against it. No row data was stored.</p>
  {{else}}<p class="empty">The inspected objects match for the checks listed below. This does not mean that row data or every database property is identical.</p>{{end}}
  {{end}}
</section>
{{with .History}}
<section id="object-times" class="object-times" aria-labelledby="object-times-heading">
  <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="object-times-heading">Object modification times</h2><p>{{len .Objects}} current object(s)</p></div>
  <p class="subtitle">SQL Server local metadata times, newest first. Table/view timestamps can change for index DDL even when the compared schema is unchanged. These are not row-change times or a complete DDL history.</p>
  <table class="inventory timestamps">
    <caption>Current objects — removed objects appear in Differences</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Object / type</th><th scope="col">Created</th><th scope="col">Last modified</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{{range .Objects}}
      <tr><th scope="row"><code>{{.Object}}</code><span class="kind">{{.Type}}</span></th><td>{{.CreatedAt}}</td><td>{{.ModifiedAt}}</td></tr>
    {{else}}<tr><td colspan="3">No objects in the comparison scope.</td></tr>{{end}}</tbody>
  </table>
</section>
{{end}}
<section id="scope" class="scope" aria-labelledby="scope-heading">
  <h2 id="scope-heading">Scope and interpretation</h2>
  <p><strong>Compared:</strong> user tables; column names, types and nullability; primary-key columns, order, direction and clustering; SQL procedure, view and function definitions with ANSI_NULLS and QUOTED_IDENTIFIER; synonym target names; CLR scalar/table-valued functions (FS/FT) by assembly identity/permission set/main-DLL SHA-256, class/method, ordered parameter/default/return signatures, EXECUTE AS and NULL ON NULL INPUT.</p>
  <p><strong>Not compared:</strong> row data, table column order/defaults/identity/computed expressions/collation, non-PK indexes, FK/CHECK/UNIQUE constraints, constraint names, triggers, object GRANT/DENY permissions, type/XML schema definitions and other advanced properties. CLR dependency assemblies, ancillary assembly files and instance-level CLR settings are excluded.</p>
  <p>Names are case-sensitive. SQL hunks show the original definitions. In normalized mode, ignored declaration changes can appear alongside other differences. Synonym targets are compared by name, not by connecting to the referenced object.</p>
  <p>CLR metadata is compared independently of SQL mode; it is not a T-SQL definition diff. Missing or changed CLR functions require manual assembly/function migration.</p>
  {{if .Offline}}<p>Both inputs were validated as supported schema snapshots. Database permissions, readable definitions and CLR metadata were required when each snapshot was captured, not during this offline comparison. Snapshots contain only their documented comparison scope, not a complete database backup or DDL audit.</p>
  {{else}}<p>Encrypted or unreadable SQL definitions/CLR metadata and unsupported CLR procedures (PC), aggregates (AF) or extended procedures (X) cause an error rather than being silently skipped. Database-level VIEW DEFINITION and readable CLR assembly bytes are required; object-level DENY can hide metadata. {{if .History}}Avoid concurrent schema changes: metadata is read in multiple queries, not a transactionally consistent snapshot.{{else}}Avoid concurrent schema changes because the databases are read sequentially.{{end}}</p>{{end}}
</section>
<footer>Generated by dbcp. This file works offline with no scripts or external assets. SQL definitions may contain sensitive values; share the report accordingly.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
